# Filename Convention

When creating a new file in any numbered track folder (`0. Software Engineering/` through `11. Harness Engineering/`), follow this convention.

## Numbered notes

Pattern: `X.Y. Title Case.md`

| Element | Rule | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `X` | Track number, matches the folder | `7` for `7. AI System Architecture` |
| `.Y` | Note number within the track, sequential, no gaps | `.3` if `7.1` and `7.2` already exist |
| `. ` | Period then real space (not hyphen, not underscore) | — |
| `Title Case` | Each significant word capitalized, real spaces | `Claude Platform Managed Agent` |
| `— Subtitle` | Em-dash (U+2014) + space + Title Case subtitle, optional | `Self-Implemented Agent Harness — Components` |
| `.md` | Lowercase extension | — |

Full example: `7.2. Self-Implemented Agent Harness — Components.md`.

## Stubs

For not-yet-promoted placeholders (one-liners, sketches), use `lowercase-hyphenated.md`:

- `prompt-caching.md`
- `fine-grained-tool-streaming.md`

Stubs get **promoted** to numbered notes (`X.Y. Title Case.md`) once they reach the ~150-line, References-section-included threshold.

## Track READMEs

Each track folder contains exactly one `README.md`. It is the entry point for the track and lists the numbered notes with one-sentence summaries.

## Before you create a new file

1. Confirm the track number (`X`) by reading the parent folder name.
2. Find the highest existing `X.Y` in the folder; new note is `X.(Y+1)`.
3. URL-encode spaces (`%20`) when cross-linking from other notes.
4. After creating the file, update the track `README.md` to list it.

## Forbidden

- Renaming or moving existing numbered notes without explicit user confirmation. Renames break cross-link URLs across the repo.
- Creating a new top-level track folder (`12. …`) without explicit user confirmation.
